  "findings": [
    {
      "headline": "The control is the worst arm on general30, not the baseline.",
      "detail": "control general30: 17 of 30 acoustically collapsed, median distinct 4, modal top token 1316 at a 0.90-0.91 share - the same 1316/768/318 texture that fills the teacher-forced silent partner stream. The same control on held-out and seen is clean (0 of 10 and 0 of 10, median distinct 57 and 65), so this is a property of the general30 prompts, not of the checkpoint."
    },
    {
      "headline": "The audio collapse is monotone in epoch on the voice prompt sets.",
      "detail": "V-real held-out acoustic collapses run 0, 0, 1, 8, 8 across epochs 1-5 and V-tts 0, 0, 0, 3, 4. The text-side silence counts tell the same story one epoch later, which is what a knife-edge test does to a graded failure."
    },
    {
      "headline": "V-real epoch 1 collapses in text while its audio stays varied.",
      "detail": "Epoch 1 has 20 monologue and 50 repeat failures over 50 generations and 0 acoustic collapses, with median distinct 42-50. Neither half of the detector subsumes the other."
    }
  ],
